// ControlledByYou = the generic "<X> you control" filter shape (the
// controller-restriction idiom behind anthem effects and the general
// "you control" postnominal restriction): wraps any base quality
// `Param(0)` with the controller-is-you relation, mirroring the
// already-lexicalized `OtherCreatureYouControl`/`CreatureOpponentControls`
// siblings (`body: And([Creature, ... ControlledBy(...)])`) but
// parameterized over the base predicate instead of fixing it to `Creature`.
// `Predicate::And(Arc<[Predicate]>)` and
// `RelationPredicate::ControlledBy(Arc<Predicate>)`
// (`crates/deckmaste_core/src/filter.rs`) are the exact pairing
// `OtherCreatureYouControl.ron`/`CreatureOpponentControls.ron` already use.
//
// The frame `<Param(0)> you control` claims the nominal's `complements`
// field (the frame's own "you control"), leaving the hole with
// `modifiers`+`head` — the mirror image of `target <Param(0)>` (frame
// claims `determiner`, hole takes the rest). See `field_slice()` in
// `crates/deckmaste_spelling/src/compile.rs`.
//
// Named distinctly from the existing `Condition`-kind `YouControl`
// (`plugins/builtin/macros/condition/YouControl.ron`, "you control ${0}",
// prenominal, unrelated body `Exists(And([Param(0), ControlledBy(Ref(You))]))`):
// `cargo xtask macro inspect` resolves a macro by name alone across every
// loaded macro (`crates/xtask/src/macros/inspect.rs`) with no kind
// disambiguation, so two same-named macros in different kinds make
// `macro inspect` non-deterministic about which one it reports — a
// pre-existing latent hazard (`Draw`/`Draws` share names across
// `EventFilter` and `OneShotEffect`+`KeywordAction`, and `Creature` across
// `Predicate` and `TypeDef`) that a fresh macro should not add another
// instance of.
(
    name: "ControlledByYou",
    template: "${0} you control",
    kinds: [Predicate],
    params: [Predicate],
    frames: ["<Param(0)> you control"],
    body: And([Param(0), ControlledBy(Ref(You))]),
)
